! Face-centred-cubic nickel with its moment along a THREE-FOLD axis, (1,1,1),
! noncollinear and without spin-orbit coupling. The cell exists for one reason:
! it is the only committed input whose spin rotations are neither diagonal nor
! symmetric, and that is what a symmetrised spinor projection has to be pinned
! against.
!
! `ni-ldau-noncol.in` is the same crystal with the moment along `z`, and it
! cannot do this job. Every one of its sixteen operations turns the spin about
! `z` alone, so its 2x2 spinor matrix is diagonal, its phase factors out of a
! modulus, and the projection comes out identical whether the spin factor is
! the right matrix, its transpose, its conjugate or the identity -- a check
! whose clean agreement cannot be told from doing nothing at all. Turning the
! moment onto (1,1,1) keeps twelve operations, six of them with time reversal,
! and six of the twelve mix the two spin components with `|U - U^T| = 1`.
!
! What it then measures, against the same cell at `nosym` on the closed 4x4x4
! grid: the wedge's Loewdin charges are 1.1e-5 electrons from the closed grid's
! with the symmetrisation on and 5.4e-2 without it, and the three arrangements
! of the spin factor that are not `conj(U)` -- `U`, `U^T` and `U^dagger` -- sit
! at 3.9e-2, 2.1e-2 and 2.1e-2, which is worse than not symmetrising the spin
! at all. The Hubbard `U` of the other file is dropped: it costs iterations and
! changes nothing about the projection.
!
! The angles are the (1,1,1) direction exactly -- `angle1 = acos(1/sqrt(3))` in
! degrees, `angle2 = 45` -- and they have to be, since the three-fold operation
! survives only for a moment on the axis itself.
&control
      calculation = 'scf'
   /
   &system
      ibrav = 2
      celldm(1) = 6.65
      nat = 1
      ntyp = 1
      ecutwfc = 25.0
      ecutrho = 200.0
      occupations = 'smearing'
      smearing = 'mv'
      degauss = 0.02
      noncolin = .true.
      starting_magnetization(1) = 0.5
      angle1(1) = 54.735610317245346
      angle2(1) = 45.0
   /
   &electrons
      conv_thr = 1.d-9
      mixing_beta = 0.3
      electron_maxstep = 200
   /
   ATOMIC_SPECIES
   Ni 58.6934 Ni.pz-nd-rrkjus.UPF
   ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
   Ni  0.00  0.00  0.00
   K_POINTS automatic
   4 4 4 0 0 0
